flowchart TB
    accTitle: The complete CoALA decision cycle
    accDescr: Current working information enters a planning stage. Planning contains proposal, evaluation, and selection, with flexible relationships rather than one mandated internal order. Execution applies a selected external grounding action or internal learning action. An observation may follow external grounding, and the decision procedure continues into another cycle.

    WM[Current working information]
    PLAN[Planning stage<br/>Proposal • Evaluation • Selection<br/>flexible internal relationships]
    EXEC[Execution<br/>apply selected procedure]
    GROUND[External grounding action]
    LEARN[Internal learning action]
    OBS[Possible environmental observation]
    NEXT[Information available for the next cycle]
    WM --> PLAN --> EXEC
    EXEC --> GROUND
    EXEC --> LEARN
    GROUND -. observation may be available .-> OBS
    OBS --> NEXT
    LEARN --> NEXT
    NEXT --> WM

    classDef process fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef action fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.1px;
    classDef result fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.4px;
    class WM,PLAN,EXEC process;
    class GROUND,LEARN action;
    class OBS,NEXT result;
